    {
      "title": "Reign of the Archfiend Event Ends",
      "anchor": "Reign_of_the_Archfiend_Event_Ends",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "The Ratatoskr update is your last chance to buy all of the Reign of the Archfiend event at a discount.",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "This can be found in the Store > Special tab for this update"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "It is also the final update where Wyrm Seals can be collected to unlock rewards, such as Grovebound Mordred or The Archfiend Saga"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "The Travelers and Saga in Reign of the Archfiend will be available for individual purchase after the event concludes, but this is your final chance to get bonus rewards and the buy-all discount."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "title": "Gameplay",
      "anchor": "Gameplay",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Leaving and Returning Penalty Update"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "The first draft of the system was too sensitive to players leaving games, and then later returning. If you return, you likely left due to something out of your control and should not be punished as harshly."
            },
            {
              "text": "This has been adjusted so players will not earn Leaver Points if they return to the match within a longer, more reasonable amount of time that should allow for restarts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Dodged Lobby High Priority Queue"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "If a lobby fails due to a player dodging the Lobby, all other players can requeue with high priority matchmaking",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "This will remember your priority in the queue prior to the failed lobby, and will re-enter you to the matchmaking pool with the same priority."
                },
                {
                  "text": "This should result in a quick new lobby, with roughly the same matchmaking quality as the lobby which failed"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "For those working through Low Priority Queues, this will also allow you to remain in queue after a failed lobby without needing to wait through the Low Priority Queue again. Waiting for 5 games is appropriate, waiting for a lot more due to failed lobbies is too much."
            },
            {
              "text": "The intent is for this system to auto-requeue you after a failed lobby, but this is not fully implemented for this update"
            },
            {
              "text": "This only works for the queue you were in. (You can't skip the line for a different queue.)"
            },
            {
              "text": "If there are any party member changes, you lose High Priority. This is to prevent people bypassing a queue."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "subsections": []
    },
